                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d_{dR} \int_0^1 \psi^*_t  \iota_{\partial_t}
                    P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A}) d t
                    \&amp; =
                    \\int_0^1 d_{dR}  \psi^*_t  \iota_{\partial_t}
                    P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A}) d t
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\int_0^1 \psi^*_t  d_{dR}   \iota_{\partial_t}
                    P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A}) d t
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\int_0^1 \psi^*_t  \frac{d}{d t}
                    P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A}) d t
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\int_0^1 \left(\frac{d}{d t}
                    P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A})\right)(t) d t
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\psi^*_1 P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A})
                    \-
                    \\psi^*_0 P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A})
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    P(F_{A_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{A_1})
                    \-
                    P(F_{A_0} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{A_0})
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h3#explicit_formulas Explicit formulas
          %p
            Above we saw that a general expression for the Chern-Simons
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS_P(A_0,A_1)
            obtained from a path of connections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS_P(A_0, A_1) = \int_{[0,1]} P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A})
                  \\,.
          %p We now unwind this to get explicit formulas for the Chern-Simons form in terms of wedge products of connection forms and their curvatures.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            a pure shift path,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A : t \mapsto A_t
            notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi t
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_{\hat A}(t) = F_{A_t} + (\partial_t A_t) \wedge d t
                  \\,.
          %p Inserting this into the above expression yields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mn 1
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi t
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi t
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS_P(A_0,A_1)
                  \=
                  \\int_0^1 P(\partial_t A \wedge F_{A_t} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{A_t})
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notably if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 = 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            is the
            %em constant
            path
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi t
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A : t \mapsto t A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1  := A
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi t
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi dR
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi t
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mn 2
                          %mo −
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  F_{\hat A}
                  \&amp;= t d_{dR} A + t^2 [A \wedge A]
                  \\\
                  \&amp;=
                  t F_A + (t^2 - t) [A \wedge A]
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p this yields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mn 1
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS_P(A)
                  \:=
                  \\int_0^1 P(A \wedge (t F_{A} + (t^2 - t) [A \wedge A]))
                  \\wedge \cdots (t F_{A} + (t^2 - t) [A \wedge A])))
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is just an integral over a polynomial in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            with constant coefficients in forms. Peforming the integral yields a bunch of coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            and with these the Chern-Simons form achieves the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS(A)
                  \=
                  c_1 \langle A \wedge F_A \wedge \cdots \wedge F_A \rangle
                  +
                  c_2 \langle A \wedge [A \wedge A] \wedge F_A \wedge \cdots F_A \rangle
                  +
                  \\cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            Particularly for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            and using the definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A = d_{dR} A + [A \wedge A]
            we get
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS(A)
                  \=
                  \\langle A \wedge d A\rangle
                  +
                  c \langle A \wedge [A \wedge A]\rangle
                  \\,.
          %h3#gauged_paths_of_connections Gauged paths of connections
          %p
            Above we defined
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(A_0,A_1)
            for every path of connections form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            which is
            %em pure shift
            \. This is a possibly convenient but unnecessary restriction:
          %p
            Notice that a general (gauged) path is a general 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A \in \Omega^1(U \times [0,1], \mathfrak{g})
            which we can decompose in the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi t
                  %mo +
                  %mi λ
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat A : t \mapsto  A_t + \lambda d t
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda d t
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            defines an element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and shift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi t
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial_t A)_t
            of the connection along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            is now relative to the gauge transformation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            induced by this function: the curvature 2-form now is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi t
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi t
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_{\hat A}
                  \: t \mapsto
                  F_{A_t}
                  +
                  ((\partial_t A)_t + d_U \lambda(t) + [\lambda,A_t]) \wedge d t
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The Chern-Simons form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{[0,1]} P(F_{\hat A} \wedge \cdots \wedge F_{\hat A})
              defined with respect to any gauged lift of a pure shift path of connections differs from that of the pure shift path by an exact term.
          %h2#InInfCSTheory
            In
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We discuss now a more encompassing perspective on Chern-Simons forms the way it occurs in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
          %h3#PrerequisitesHigher Prerequisites
          %p We need to collect a few notions described elsewhere, on which the following discussion is based.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            or more generally an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            we have the following
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
            %li
              %p
                the algebra of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi inv
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inv(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            Given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            to degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            which is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncation"} truncation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi dgAlg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\mathfrak{g}) :  U,[n] \mapsto
                  dgAlg(
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}),
                  C^\infty(U)\otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^n)
                  )
                  \\,,
          %p
            where here and in the following
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^n)
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            dg-algebra of those smooth
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
