            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            of sheaves under the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
          %h3#HigherOrderChernSimonsForms Higher order Chern-Simons form
          %p With all of the above in hand, we can make now the following observations:
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a smooth manifold and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            with coefficient for pseudo-connections being
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
            as above, a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A : X \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
          %p
            of simplicial presheaves (no resolution on the left, since we are concentrating on globally defined forms for the present purpose) is effectively a
            = succeed "-values" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            a cocycle on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
            a corresponding invariant polynomial the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi diff
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi chn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff} \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
          %p
            discussed above produces the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo →
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\nabla \to \nabla') : X \cdot \Delta[1] \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
          %p
            is a smooth path in the space of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi chn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi chn
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X \cdot \Delta[1], \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}]
                  \\simeq
                  [X, \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}^{\Delta[1]}]
          %p
            this corresponds to a
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            this is the Chern-Simons form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo →
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi chn
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CS(\nabla \to \nabla') : X \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}^{\Delta[1]}
                  \\,.
          %p The higher homotopies are higher order Chern-Simons forms.
          %p The following proposition says this in a more precise way for ordinary Chern-Simons forms.
          %h4#OrdinaryCSRevisited Ordinary Chern-Simons forms revisited
          %p
            We now show how the
            %a{:href => "#PathsOfConnections"} traditional definition
            of Chern-Simons forms is reproduced by the
            %a{:href => "#HigherOrderChernSimonsForms"} general abstract
            mechanism.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (ordinary Chern-Simons form)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle \in W(\mathfrak{g})
              an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %p Then morphisms (of simplicial presheaves)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A : X \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
            %p
              are in canonical bijection with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-algebra+valued+1-forms"} Lie-algebra valued 1-forms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(X,\mathfrak{g})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
            %p
              are in canonical bijection with closed
              = succeed "-forms" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and composition with the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}G_{diff} \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
            %p
              discussed
              %a{:href => "#PrerequisitesHigher"} above
              and under this canonical identification the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle F_A \rangle : X \stackrel{A}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{B}G_{diff} \stackrel{}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
            %p
              is the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
            %p Homotopies
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi γ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A_1 \stackrel{\gamma}{\to} A_2)  : X\times \Delta[1] \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
            %p
              are in canonical bijection with smooth paths in the space of
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and under composition with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff} \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}
              these identify with the corresponding Chern-Simons form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi CS
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi γ
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle F_A\rangle
                    \\stackrel{CS(A \stackrel{\gamma}{\to} A')}{\to}
                    \\langle F_{A'}\rangle
                    \:
                    X \to (\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn})^{\Delta[1]}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p This is a straightforward unwinding of the definitions. We spell it out in the following in order to highlight the way the mechanism works.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              and the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
              is equivalently a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C^\infty(X) \otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^0) &amp;\leftarrow&amp; CE(\mathfrak{g})
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^\bullet(X) \otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^0)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{(A,F_A)}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    W(\mathfrak{g})
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              is trivial in degree 0 and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} otimess
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)\otimess \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^0)
              is trivial above degree 0, the top morphism is necessarily 0 and the commutativity of the diagram is an empty condition.
            %p
              The bottom morphism on the other hand enccodes precisely a
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            %p
              Composition with the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff} \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
              is composition of the bottom morphism of the above digram with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow CE(b^{k-1}\mathbb{R}) : \langle - \rangle
              followed by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
              of the resulting
              = succeed "-form" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet(X)\otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^0)
                    \\stackrel{(A,F_A)}{\leftarrow}
                    W(\mathfrak{g})
                    \\stackrel{\langle - \rangle}{\leftarrow}
                    CE(b^{k-1}\mathbb{R})
                    \:
                    \\langle F_A \rangle
            %p
              over the point. This fiber integration is of course trivial, so that we find that indeed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} langlw
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi chn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{(A,F_A)}{\to} \mathbf{B}G_{diff} \stackrel{\langlw - \rangle}{\to} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^k \mathbb{R}_{chn}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
              defined on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              Next, a homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi γ
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \stackrel{\gamma}{\to} A') : X \cdot \Delta[1] \to \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
              is (again by the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mi λ
                          %mtd
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi γ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ′
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C^\infty(X) \otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^1)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\lambda}{\leftarrow}&amp; CE(\mathfrak{g})
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^\bullet(X) \otimes \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^0)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{(A,F_A) \stackrel{\gamma}{\to} (A',F_{A'})}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    W(\mathfrak{g})
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The top morphism defines an
              = succeed "-parameterized" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X \times [0,1] \to G
              into the simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              = succeed "]" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} integrating
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              based at the identity,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x,0) = e
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda = g^* \theta
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \in \Omega^1(G, \mathfrak{g})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p
              or conversely by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi d
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f(x,s) = P \exp(\int_{[0,s]} \lambda(x,s) d s)
            %p
              We may think of this as a smooth
              %em path of gauge transformations
              \.
            %p
              The bottom morphism encodes a
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo +
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat A + \lambda \in \Omega^1(X \times [0,1] , \mathfrak{g})
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A \in \Omega^1(X,\mathfrak{g}) \otimes C^\infty([0,1])
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              as before, such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A(s = 0) = A
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A(s = 1) = A'
            %p
              This is a
              %em smooth path in the space of 1-forms
              \. In the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda = 0
              this is a
              %em pure shift path
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#PathsOfConnections"} terminology above
            %p
              Under composition with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow CE(b^{k-1}\mathbb{R}) : \langle -\rangle
              this becomes a
              = succeed "-form" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\langle F_{\hat A } \rangle \in \Omega^{k}(X)\otimes C^\infty(\Delta^1)\oplus \Omega^{k-1}(X)\otimes \Omega^1(\Delta^1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
              of this over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1
              is manifestly the same operation as that in the definition of the Chern-Simons form
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#PathsOfConnections"} above
          %h2#as_secondary_characteristic_forms As secondary characteristic forms
          %p
            If a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
            %em vanishes
            (for instance if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            is flat or the degree of the curvature characteristic form is simply greater than the dimension of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+form"} closed form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            class of the curvature characteristic form becomes trivial, but the Chern-Simons form provides another de Rham class. This is therefore called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/secondary+characteristic+class"} secondary characteristic class
          %h3#chernsimons_theory Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            In particular on a 3-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            necessarily the Chern-Simons 3-form is closed. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional"} functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A \in \Omega^1(X,\mathfrak{g}))
                  \\mapsto
                  \\int_X CS(A)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            called
            = succeed "." do
